      "strengths_deep_dive": [
        "UMR's operational model is built on high-volume distribution and strategic partnerships. The organization reported <cite id=\"16\">$7.1 million in foreign grants</cite> in FY2023, primarily supporting relief efforts in crisis zones. Their <cite id=\"17\">Gold Seal of Transparency from Candid</cite> reflects a commitment to public disclosure. Furthermore, the charity's <cite id=\"18\">fundraising efficiency of $0.02 to $0.02 per $1 raised</cite> ensures that the vast majority of resources are directed toward field operations rather than administrative overhead."
      ],
      "summary": "United Mission For Relief And Development (UMR) is a large-scale humanitarian organization that focuses on building resilience in underserved communities globally. Founded in <cite id=\"1\">2013</cite>, the charity has rapidly expanded its operations, reporting <cite id=\"2\">$57,586,233 in total revenue in FY2023</cite>. The organization maintains a <cite id=\"3\">94.5/100 overall score from Charity Navigator</cite>, reflecting strong performance in accountability and leadership. UMR operates across several critical sectors, including <cite id=\"4\">healthcare, water sanitation (WASH), and orphan sponsorship</cite>. While the organization reports a <cite id=\"5\">96.5% program expense ratio</cite>, donors should note that the <cite id=\"6\">cash-adjusted program ratio is 48%</cite> due to the high volume of noncash (in-kind) contributions. Despite this accounting nuance, UMR demonstrates high operational efficiency, spending only <cite id=\"7\">$0.05 to raise every $1</cite>. The charity is <cite id=\"8\">Zakat-eligible</cite> and serves multiple asnaf categories, making it a primary choice for Muslim donors seeking to fulfill religious obligations through <cite id=\"9\">direct service delivery</cite> in regions like <cite id=\"10\">Palestine, Yemen, and Sudan</cite>.",
